    "summary": "Subclassing & Super()",
    "content": "### Class Inheritance & Method Resolution Order\n\nInheritance permits a child class to inherit attributes and methods from a parent class, facilitating code reuse.\n\n#### Syntax & Mechanics\n```python\nclass ChildClass(ParentClass):\n    def __init__(self, args):\n        super().__init__(args)\n```\n- **`super()`**: Delegates method calls to the parent class.\n- **Method Overriding**: Redefining a parent method in the child class.\n- **MRO (Method Resolution Order)**: The C3 linearization algorithm determining method lookup order in multiple inheritance (`Class.mro()`).\n",
    "exampleCode": "class User:\n    def __init__(self, username: str, email: str):\n        self.username = username\n        self.email = email\n\n    def get_role_permissions(self) -> str:\n        return \"Basic Viewer\"\n\nclass Faculty(User):\n    def __init__(self, username: str, email: str, department: str):\n        super().__init__(username, email)\n        self.department = department\n\n    def get_role_permissions(self) -> str:\n        return f\"Instructor in {self.department} (Course Author & Grading)\"\n\nprof = Faculty(\"m_vance\", \"vance@learnflow.edu\", \"Computer Science\")\nprint(\"User:\", prof.username)\nprint(\"Permissions:\", prof.get_role_permissions())",
