    "summary": "Protocols & Generators",
    "content": "### Iteration Protocol & Generator Functions\n\nAn **iterator** is an object representing a stream of data that responds to the `__next__()` method.\n\n#### Protocols\n1. **Iterable**: Implements `__iter__()` returning an iterator.\n2. **Iterator**: Implements `__next__()` returning successive items or raising `StopIteration`.\n3. **Generators**: Functions containing `yield` statements that maintain execution state lazily between calls.\n",
    "exampleCode": "# Custom Fibonacci generator\ndef fibonacci(limit: int):\n    a, b = 0, 1\n    count = 0\n    while count < limit:\n        yield a\n        a, b = b, a + b\n        count += 1\n\nfib_seq = list(fibonacci(7))\nprint(\"Fibonacci first 7 numbers:\", fib_seq)",
