    "content": "### Exception Handling & Resource Management\n\nRobust software must gracefully intercept runtime errors using `try`, `except`, `else`, and `finally` blocks.\n\n#### Structure\n- **`try`**: Code that may raise an exception.\n- **`except SpecificError as e`**: Intercepts and recovers from specific exception types.\n- **`else`**: Runs ONLY if no exceptions were thrown in the try block.\n- **`finally`**: ALWAYS executes regardless of exceptions, ideal for closing file descriptors or releasing database connections.\n- **Context Managers (`with`)**: Automatically manage resource acquisition and release via `__enter__` and `__exit__`.\n",
    "exampleCode": "def safe_divide(numerator: float, denominator: float):\n    try:\n        result = numerator / denominator\n    except ZeroDivisionError as err:\n        print(\"Error intercepted:\", err)\n        return None\n    except TypeError as err:\n        print(\"Invalid types passed:\", err)\n        return None\n    else:\n        print(\"Division completed successfully.\")\n        return result\n    finally:\n        print(\"Cleanup routine executed.\")\n\nprint(\"Safe result:\", safe_divide(10, 2))\nprint(\"Zero divisor:\", safe_divide(10, 0))",
