    "summary": "Centroids, Inertia & Elbow Method",
    "content": "### K-Means Clustering: Unsupervised Partitioning\n\nK-Means partitions \\(n\\) unlabeled observations into \\(k\\) clusters where each observation belongs to the cluster with the nearest mean (cluster centroid).\n\n#### The Expectation-Maximization Algorithm\n1. **Initialize**: Randomly choose \\(k\\) centroids in feature space.\n2. **Assignment Step**: Assign each observation to its nearest centroid (Euclidean distance).\n3. **Update Step**: Recompute the coordinates of each centroid as the arithmetic mean of all points assigned to that cluster.\n4. **Repeat** until centroids stabilize (convergence).\n\n#### Choosing \\(k\\): The Elbow Method\nPlot **Inertia** (Within-Cluster Sum of Squares) against \\(k\\); the optimal cluster count is located at the point where the rate of decrease abruptly shifts (the 'elbow').\n",
