    "content": "### Model Evaluation: Metrics & Validation\n\nAccuracy alone is deceptive on imbalanced datasets (e.g. fraud detection where 99.9% of transactions are legitimate).\n\n#### Classification Metrics\n- **Confusion Matrix**: True Positive (TP), False Positive (FP), False Negative (FN), True Negative (TN).\n- **Precision**: \\(\text{TP} / (\text{TP} + \text{FP})\\) (Of all predicted positives, how many were correct?).\n- **Recall (Sensitivity)**: \\(\text{TP} / (\text{TP} + \text{FN})\\) (Of all actual positives, how many did the model catch?).\n- **F1-Score**: Harmonic mean of Precision and Recall:\n  \\[\n  F_1 = 2 \\cdot \frac{\text{Precision} \\cdot \text{Recall}}{\text{Precision} + \text{Recall}}\n  \\]\n\n#### K-Fold Cross Validation\nSplits dataset into \\(k\\) folds, training on \\(k-1\\) and testing on the remaining fold, repeating \\(k\\) times to assess generalization variance.\n",
